## Frequently asked questions

**Do you only work with Cardiff businesses?**

No. We work with businesses across South Wales and the UK, but Cardiff is one of our core service areas. We also cover [Swansea](/web-design-swansea/), [Newport](/web-design-newport/), and [Merthyr Tydfil](/web-design-merthyr-tydfil/).

**Can you help improve my Google rankings?**

Yes. Every website we build is SEO-ready from day one. We also offer dedicated [local SEO campaigns for Cardiff businesses](/seo-cardiff/) for those who want to go further.

**How long does a website take?**

Most projects are completed within 7–14 days depending on scope and how quickly we receive content from you.

**Will my website work on mobile?**

Yes. Every website we build uses mobile-first design — it will look and perform perfectly on phones, tablets, and desktops.

**Can I update the site myself?**

Yes. We build on platforms that give you full access to manage your own content, and we provide training as part of every project.

**Do you build ecommerce websites in Cardiff?**

Yes — we build custom ecommerce stores using Shopify, WooCommerce, and SureCart. See our [ecommerce web design Cardiff](/ecommerce-web-design-cardiff/) page for more details.

**How much does web design in Cardiff cost?**

Our WordPress web design service starts from £199 for a one-page website. We also offer managed monthly website packages from £20/month inc. VAT for smaller starter sites. The right option depends on how many pages you need, whether you need copywriting, and whether you want SEO support included.

**Can you build an affordable Cardiff website that still ranks?**

Yes. The budget affects the scope, not the foundations. Even a smaller website should have clear headings, fast loading, proper page titles, local wording, and a structure that makes sense to Google.

**Do you build websites for Cardiff trades and service businesses?**

Yes. We work with trades, professional services, local service businesses, ecommerce brands, and start-ups across Cardiff. The page structure is planned around the services and areas that matter most to your business.

